// Propulsion. PLACEHOLDER NUMBERS, all for feel only: engine thrust and rated speeds were set on 12 Oct 2026 for
// the agility target "Agile" (GDR-0042: 0 → ~22 m/s in ~2.5 s), about 16× the concept-board thrust; the gyro
// torque and the RCS thrust on 13 Oct 2026 for slower, crisper turning (GDR-0055: Halvex Runner 90° in ~1.5 s,
// gyros moderate, RCS pods the strong turners); gimbal values are invented.
// Engines push towards the part's forward side and may sit anywhere (GDR-0039); `gimbal` swings their thrust a
// few degrees to either side. `rated_speed` (GDR-0041, GDR-0055): while it pushes with the ship's motion, the
// thrust fades out as the ship's whole speed approaches it, so the fastest engines set the top speed. `plume`
// (GDR-0039, GDR-0049): the exhaust reaches `length` m behind the engine and burns the first part in its path (the
// ship's own, enemies and wrecks; never other vessels of the same owner) with `damage` and `heat` per second at
// full thrust, scaled by the thrust it gives. PLACEHOLDER plume numbers (lead, 12 Oct 2026): a torch drive held on
// a raider for about a second wrecks a part or two; an engine buried in the hull burns through an armour block in
// a second or two. Gyros turn the ship without thrust; RCS pods fire a nozzle out of every side that is open to
// space (they have no plume), and two nozzles of opposite sides firing together turn the ship without pushing it.
// Power tier: everything that moves the ship is `Normal` (the default), so thrust and turning brown out together.
// `salvage`: what the part gives when salvaged and dismantled at home (research data about its build points;
// PLACEHOLDER, lead defaults of 13 Oct 2026 after docs/plans/first-playable-loop.md 3.2).
